  "usage_note": "**Development** is uncountable when it means growth (*a child's development*), making something new (*software development*), or the work of building on land (*land for development*). It is countable when it means a new event (*a new development*) or a group of new buildings (*a housing development*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Many development countries need clean water.",
      "correct": "Many developing countries need clean water.",
      "note": "Before **country** or **nation**, use the adjective **developing**, not the noun **development**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "There is a new develop in the story.",
      "correct": "There is a new development in the story.",
      "note": "**Develop** is the verb; the noun for a new event is **development**."
    }
  ],
